01:44:25.270 --> 01:44:41.880
Prof. John Tsitsiklis: a particular individual, and we have to do that for each one of the particular individuals. So that's computationally expensive. It turns out that for linear regression, ordinary, least squares, there's some computational shortcuts, but otherwise it is very expensive.

552
01:44:42.650 --> 01:44:57.309
